1. Running a important script? Don't want anyone to interrupt it? add this to the top of the script
bashtrap '' 2
# or
trap '' SIGINT
After that, if it less important lines in the script, use this to bring back SIGINT
bashtrap - 2
# or
trap - SIGINT

2. Put this at the top of the script and it will delete the fail when the script is stopped
bashtrap "rm -f $filename" EXIT

3. To catch SIGINT until the count is over
bashint_count=0

function stop_it()
{
    let int_count++
    echo
    if [[ $int_count == 1 ]]; then
        echo "I am not going to quit"
    elif [[ $int_count == 2 ]]; then
        echo "If you do that again, ill exit"
    elif [[ $int_count == 3 ]]; then
        echo "You are fooled!"
    else
        echo "Bye"
        exit
    fi
}

